# Leave both unset for local dev without a backend — the app falls back to
# its own mock API routes under /api/* (see src/lib/store.ts). But if the
# real backend is up (it is), copy this file to .env.local and fill these
# in, or the app will silently mock everything with no obvious error.
#
# The Floater is deployed on Heroku as of 2026-08-09; point at it to talk to
# the real backend. Swap for the custom domain once Infra wires up DNS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://testbench-api-53f53b05d813.herokuapp.com

# R2 public bucket domain, live as of 2026-08-09. Nothing in the app reads
# this var yet (no screen displays the original uploaded file), but it's
# here so it's ready when that lands.
NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_PUBLIC_BASE=https://pub-42861a7682c8422c854d3698618e8987.r2.dev
